    "70": "Let \\((\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma)\\) be the foot of perpendicular from the point \\((1,2,3)\\) on the line \\(\\frac{x+3}{5}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{3}\\). Then \\(19(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)\\) is equal to:",
    "72": "If the domain of the function \\(f(x)=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2-|x|}{4}\\right)+\\left(\\log_{e}(3-x)\\right)^{-1}\\) is \\([-\\alpha,\\beta)-\\{\\gamma\\}\\), then \\(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma\\) is equal to:",
    "73": "Consider the system of linear equations \\(x+y+z=4\\mu,\\ x+2y+2\\lambda z=10\\mu,\\ x+3y+4\\lambda^{2}z=\\mu^{2}+15\\), where \\(\\lambda,\\mu\\in R\\). Which one of the following statements is NOT correct?"
